Fix SPARC JDK17 crash: guarantee(_post_Java_sp != NULL) failed: bad stack!

On SPARC 64-bit, JavaFrameAnchor::capture_last_Java_pc() calls
frame::next_younger_sp_or_null(last_Java_sp(), sp) and then hits
a guarantee if the result is NULL:

  guarantee(_post_Java_sp != NULL, "bad stack!")   // frame_sparc.cpp:694

This guarantee fires during G1 GC root-scan / concurrent-mark-remark when
a GC thread walks another thread's Java stack and that thread is mid-entry
into a runtime stub (e.g., _new_instance_Java allocation slow path). The
SPARC frame anchor is set up in two separate stores:

  1. last_Java_sp is written (with STACK_BIAS, per generateOptoStub.cpp)
  2. _post_Java_sp is written after the register window save completes

If a G1 safepoint fires between these two stores, next_younger_sp_or_null
returns NULL (the register windows haven't been saved yet, so the younger
frame can't be located), and the guarantee crashes the VM.

The fix replaces the guarantee with an early return: if _post_Java_sp is
NULL the stack is not yet walkable, so we return without capturing the PC
or marking windows as flushed. GC covers such threads via other root-scan
paths (oops_do, nmethods_do) which don't require a fully-initialized frame
anchor. This matches the analogous guard added to make_walkable() in jdk19.

See: https://github.com/ptribble/jdk-sunos-builder/issues/7

--- a/src/hotspot/cpu/sparc/frame_sparc.cpp
+++ b/src/hotspot/cpu/sparc/frame_sparc.cpp
@@ -686,9 +686,13 @@ void JavaFrameAnchor::capture_last_Java_pc(intptr_t* sp) {
   if (last_Java_sp() != NULL && last_Java_pc() == NULL) {
     // try and find the sp just younger than _last_Java_sp
     intptr_t* _post_Java_sp = frame::next_younger_sp_or_null(last_Java_sp(), sp);
-    // Really this should never fail otherwise VM call must have non-standard
-    // frame linkage (bad) or stack is not properly flushed (worse).
-    guarantee(_post_Java_sp != NULL, "bad stack!");
+    // If _post_Java_sp is NULL the frame anchor is partially initialized:
+    // the thread is mid-entry into a runtime stub (last_Java_sp is set but
+    // the register window save and _post_Java_sp store have not completed).
+    // Return without capturing the PC or marking windows as flushed; GC
+    // covers this thread via other root-scan paths (oops_do etc.).
+    // Mirrors the analogous guard added to make_walkable() in jdk19.
+    if (_post_Java_sp == NULL) return;
     _last_Java_pc = (address) _post_Java_sp[ I7->sp_offset_in_saved_window()] + frame::pc_return_offset;

   }
